  "goodToKnow": "Der Applaus is applause: tosender Applaus (thunderous applause), Applaus bekommen. The native German word is der Beifall: Beifall klatschen. A curious German custom: at the end of a university lecture, students often knock on their desks (klopfen) instead of clapping. Applaudieren means to applaud. At concerts, ending applause too early between movements is frowned upon."
